# Downloaded data (CUB-200-2011 archive + extracted images, ~1.2GB) and the
# cloned hierarchy repo -- both are re-fetched automatically by
# src/download_data.py and src/hierarchy.py, so committing them would just
# bloat the repo for no reason.
data/

# Trained checkpoints are too large for a normal git push (ResNet-101
# state_dict + Adam optimizer state is well over GitHub's 100MB per-file
# limit). See README.md "Checkpoints" section for why these are not
# committed and how reproduce.sh regenerates them.
checkpoints/*.pt

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
